            {"q": "What is the outbound API queue?", "a": "<code>api_queue</code> serializes outbound calls to rate-limited sources (NVD, OTX, LLM providers). <code>/api/health</code> exposes per-source queue depth so operators see waiting vs active work. Feed sync paths pass human-readable <code>operation</code> labels for the header Background sync indicator."},
            {"q": "How does the platform separate read and write paths?", "a": "Analyst GET endpoints read from Postgres and caches (<code>feed_cache</code>, <code>ioc_cache</code>). Writes flow through ingest jobs, admin config apply, or authenticated POST/PATCH routes. NVD ingest uses explicit transaction boundaries so slow enrichments cannot hold writer connections."},
            {"q": "What is Procrastinate's role relative to APScheduler?", "a": "APScheduler remains the in-process cron owner for ~27 recurring jobs. Procrastinate (optional, <code>PROCRASTINATE_ENABLED</code>) adds durable outbound jobs\u2014health ping, stack backfill, LLM product extraction\u2014with Postgres-backed retries. Most ingest still runs through APScheduler locks."},
