            {"q": "When does SQLite still appear?", "a": "SQLite is the zero-config test/dev fallback when <code>DATABASE_URL</code> is empty and Postgres is not required. CI default pytest uses SQLite; operators must run Postgres-backed tests before merging <code>db/</code> changes. Health reports <code>backend: sqlite</code> vs <code>postgresql</code>."},
            {"q": "How does the asyncpg pool work?", "a": "<code>DATABASE_POOL_SIZE</code> configures concurrent connections. Drawer bundle assembly intentionally uses separate connections per sub-fetch for safe parallelism. <code>DATABASE_POOL_COMMAND_TIMEOUT_SECONDS</code> caps SQL wait time separately from per-feed HTTP timeouts."},
            {"q": "What is <code>db/pg_adapt.py</code>?", "a": "It adapts Postgres-native SQL for SQLite compatibility in the test suite\u2014parallel <code>_SQLITE</code> / <code>_PG</code> query constants where needed. Production path is Postgres-only; do not reintroduce a generic dialect translation layer."},
            {"q": "How are migrations managed?", "a": "Alembic revisions in <code>backend/alembic/versions/</code> are forward-only. Never edit applied migrations; add a new revision. Reserved words like <code>references</code> caused real bugs\u2014prefer renamed columns over quoted identifiers."},
