            {"q": "What is <code>feed_cache</code>?", "a": "TTL JSON blobs for expensive or slow paths: OTX pulses, detection context, LLM outputs, and more. Distinct from canonical tables\u2014read paths may serve stale mirror rows on upstream 4xx/5xx without deleting cached intel."},
            {"q": "How does transaction boundary discipline work?", "a": "<code>db/txn_boundaries.py</code> ensures NVD ingest commits before CIRCL/Sploitus enrich so slow sources cannot exhaust the writer pool. Long-running jobs batch commits; request handlers keep transactions short."},
            {"q": "What indexing supports feed performance?", "a": "KEV JOIN optimizations, count caches, <code>pg_trgm</code> for search, and keyset pagination on <code>/api/cves</code> (<code>pagination=keyset</code>). ORJSON accelerates default JSON responses."},
            {"q": "How are user preferences persisted?", "a": "<code>user_preferences</code> stores display settings, timezone, and optional asset profile JSON. Stack terms use <code>GET/PUT /api/me/stack</code> with legacy localStorage migration on login."},
            {"q": "What is <code>app_settings</code>?", "a": "Writable operator config survives deploys when env vars are unset. Precedence: process env \u2192 DB \u2192 <code>.env</code>. Secret fields encrypt with <code>BRIEFR_SETTINGS_KEY</code>. Admin Save can mirror to <code>.env</code> for compatibility."},
