            {"q": "What entities get embedded?", "a": "CVEs, ATT&amp;CK techniques, and non-retracted <code>correlation_campaigns</code> (E8). <code>content_hash</code> drift triggers re-embed on scheduled backfill. Caps: ingest max 25, backfill max 2000 per run."},
            {"q": "What is <code>EMBEDDINGS_AUTO_ON_INGEST</code>?", "a": "Defaults on when embeddings enabled\u2014new/changed CVEs enqueue embed work on ingest. Admin can disable auto-on-ingest independently. CPU-only local embedding model\u2014no GPU requirement documented."},
            {"q": "How does hybrid semantic search work?", "a": "<code>/api/search/semantic</code> combines vector similarity with stack/severity/KEV filters. FEED renders Techniques / Campaigns / CVEs sections. My Stack context stays on during hybrid mode."},
            {"q": "Describe the LLM provider router.", "a": "Scheduler-side chain: Groq \u2192 Cerebras \u2192 OpenRouter free tier \u2192 Gemini, centralized in <code>ai/model_catalog.py</code>. PDF summaries and product extraction use the router. Anthropic was removed from the chain."},
            {"q": "What is LLM pacing (K5)?", "a": "<code>ai/llm_pacing.py</code> holds ~85% headroom below provider RPM/TPM ceilings. Prevents burning quotas during batch jobs. Catch-up mode raises headroom temporarily."},
            {"q": "What gets logged in <code>ai_operations</code>?", "a": "Redacted metadata per <code>chat_completion_task</code> attempt\u2014no prompt text by default. Token counts when providers return usage. Admin AI Operations page: Overview, Providers, Models, Usage, Activity tabs."},
            {"q": "How do empty LLM responses degrade?", "a": "Blank bodies count toward circuit health. Scheduler jobs use <code>llm_job_session()</code> to skip a failing provider for remaining CVEs in that run while still failing over on first empty response."},
            {"q": "What is detection context LLM (K4)?", "a": "<code>detection_context_llm</code> job extracts paths, params, keywords from CVE/exploit text into <code>feed_cache</code> keys <code>detection_ctx:{cve_id}</code>. Disabled by default (<code>DETECTION_CONTEXT_LLM_ENABLED=0</code>); restart required to register job."},
            {"q": "How does Nuclei parsing relate to ML?", "a": "Deterministic Nuclei YAML parser (D4) enriches detection context artifacts on exploit sync\u2014default on. LLM extract is an optional overlay, not the primary path."},
            {"q": "What quotas does AI-3 expose?", "a": "Advisory snapshots from provider rate-limit response headers in <code>ai/quota.py</code>. Surfaced on AI Operations provider rows and overview <code>quota_warnings</code>\u2014informational, not hard enforcement."},
            {"q": "Can admins replay failed LLM operations?", "a": "Yes\u2014Program E: view payload and <code>POST .../retry</code> with replay provenance, circuit-open guard unless <code>force=true</code>, and audit entries. Activity rows show <code>has_payload</code> when captured."},
            {"q": "Why skip LLM calls on empty text?", "a": "Cost and quota protection\u2014<code>llm_payload.py</code> enforces at router and client layers. Prevents noop provider HTTP when CVE description or exploit text is blank."},
            {"q": "What models are defaults in 2026?", "a": "OpenRouter free Gemini Flash-Lite IDs went stale; catalog SSOT updated to working IDs. Operators should clear old <code>OPENROUTER_MODEL_*</code> env overrides so defaults apply."},
            {"q": "Is vision used?", "a": "Deferred until image inputs exist in the pipeline. Router supports text tasks today; Cerebras gemma vision noted for future detection artifact extraction."},
            {"q": "How does retrieval health reporting work?", "a": "<code>GET /api/admin/retrieval/health</code> shows embedding counts by entity, pending work, extension presence, last backfill. Coupled to AI ops panel\u2014not a separate silo."},
            {"q": "What is NOT done with LLMs?", "a": "Threat/OP scores are rule-based, not LLM-generated. Generic detection dumps are suppressed. No unauthenticated summarization endpoints. LLMs assist optional enrichment and operator-facing PDF summaries."},
            {"q": "How do embeddings interact with catch-up?", "a": "Catch-up tick includes embeddings backfill when enabled, along with correlation precompute and CPE catalog sync\u2014subject to existing gates and locks."},
            {"q": "How would you answer 'why local embeddings vs API-only'?", "a": "Local CPU embeddings keep recurring cost predictable for self-hosters and avoid shipping CVE text to a third party for every search. Optional cloud LLMs remain for tasks that need generative output, with explicit operator keys."},
