            {"q": "Is full docker-compose shipped?", "a": "Postgres compose exists (<code>deploy/docker-compose.postgres.yml</code> with pgvector image). All-in-one platform compose is planned\u2014not the current production reference path."},
            {"q": "What is <code>verify-local.sh</code>?", "a": "Pre-merge gate mirroring CI: SQLite pytest, dependency audit, frontend build, unit tests, scoped lint. <code>--full</code> adds Postgres pytest, gitleaks, Playwright smoke. Green local verify suffices when GitHub Actions quota is exhausted."},
            {"q": "How are backups handled?", "a": "Scheduled backup job plus deadman check. Postgres CI runs backup round-trip test. Admin UI exposes backup status; Download DB removed for Postgres\u2014legacy SQLite export route remains dev-only."},
            {"q": "What does <code>briefr-doctor.sh</code> do?", "a": "Deploy script runs health/import checks and optional support pack download\u2014operator diagnostics on the live box without manual curl juggling."},
            {"q": "How do migrations run in deploy?", "a": "Alembic upgrade on deploy before uvicorn restart. Forward-only\u2014roll forward fixes, never edit stamped revisions. Postgres apply required before merge for DDL changes."},
            {"q": "What CI jobs exist?", "a": "test, dependency-audit, frontend build, frontend unit tests; full adds Postgres tests, gitleaks (known red), Playwright smoke. dependency-audit and gitleaks are known non-blockers per CLAUDE.md."},
            {"q": "How is nginx configured?", "a": "Serves static frontend, proxies <code>/api</code> to uvicorn on localhost. TLS typically terminates at nginx or Cloudflare tunnel\u2014not inside FastAPI."},
            {"q": "What env vars matter for ops?", "a": "<code>DATABASE_URL</code>, <code>JWT_SECRET</code>, <code>BRIEFR_REQUIRE_POSTGRES=1</code>, <code>RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=1</code>, <code>BRIEFR_SCHEDULER_ENABLED</code>, <code>BRIEFR_RATE_LIMIT_STORE=db</code> for multi-worker, <code>BRIEFR_SETTINGS_KEY</code> for encrypted settings."},
            {"q": "How do API-only workers deploy?", "a": "Multiple uvicorn instances behind nginx with <code>BRIEFR_SCHEDULER_ENABLED=0</code>; exactly one scheduler owner with <code>=1</code>. Shared DB rate-limit store mandatory for consistent auth/IOC limits."},
            {"q": "What is log rotation?", "a": "Deploy artifacts include logrotate configs for structured JSON logs\u2014journald-friendly stderr from uvicorn."},
            {"q": "How is Postgres sized?", "a": "No official sizing envelope published; architecture targets small VPS\u2014CPU embeddings, single worker, bounded pool. Operators monitor admin Resources page and host disk I/O charts."},
            {"q": "What license applies?", "a": "Apache 2.0\u2014free for personal, commercial, and self-hosted use with attribution. SPDX headers in source trees."},
            {"q": "How do intel snapshots help DR?", "a": "Export/import bundles for allowlisted intel tables\u2014versioned manifest, verify script, documented in OPERATIONS.md. Complements pg_dump backups, not a replacement."},
            {"q": "What production warnings fire at startup?", "a": "Posture self-check logs per unsafe flag when <code>BRIEFR_ENV=production</code>\u2014rate limits off, insecure cookies, tokenless wallboard. Surfaced again in Admin Security panel."},
            {"q": "How is frontend released?", "a": "<code>npm run build</code> produces <code>dist/</code> copied to nginx root on deploy. Vite dev server proxies <code>/api</code> only for development."},
            {"q": "What about Playwright smoke?", "a": "Gated behind <code>PLAYWRIGHT_SMOKE=1</code> in verify-local full mode. Seeds SQLite and starts uvicorn + preview for UI smoke\u2014optional locally."},
            {"q": "How do deploy scripts stay safe?", "a": "Additive compatibility promise in ROADMAP/OPERATIONS\u2014<code>deploy/</code> scripts run on live production boxes; changes must not break existing operator paths."},
            {"q": "What would you check after a failed deploy?", "a": "Alembic version, health endpoint backend kind, scheduler owner flag, nginx proxy, JWT/auth login, feed row count, and application logs for migration or pool errors."},
