            {"q": "Why build BRIEFR as a solo maintainer project?", "a": "I wanted analyst-grade CVE triage without SIEM cost or SaaS data residency concerns. A monolith with honest self-host docs matches how small teams actually deploy\u2014one Postgres, one operator, incremental flags instead of microservice sprawl."},
            {"q": "How do you prioritize the roadmap?", "a": "<code>docs/PRODUCT_STATUS.md</code> and <code>docs/planning/SPRINT_2026-07.md</code> drive truth. I ship operator pain first\u2014auth hardening, scheduler honesty, feed performance\u2014before greenfield features like full platform compose."},
            {"q": "Tell me about a hard technical trade-off you made.", "a": "I kept APScheduler in-process instead of jumping to Celery everywhere. Procrastinate is optional for a narrow durable queue. That trades theoretical scale for operability\u2014one lock map, one admin Scheduler page, predictable failures."},
            {"q": "How do you handle docs vs code drift?", "a": "PRODUCT_STATUS wins over README snapshots. I update SYSTEM_DESIGN and API_REFERENCE in the same PR as behavior changes. Corpus drift check in admin compares generated security architecture to committed files."},
            {"q": "Describe a production incident mindset you encoded.", "a": "RCA-first: reproduce, trace end-to-end, fix the class of bug, add a regression test. Example: FE refresh dedupe\u2014concurrent 401s could revoke all sessions; shared in-flight refresh fixed the structural race, not just retry logic."},
            {"q": "Why Apache 2.0?", "a": "Maximum adoption for defenders who cannot ship GPL contagion into commercial SOCs. Clear NOTICE attribution; aligns with SigmaHQ and ecosystem tooling expectations."},
            {"q": "How do you say no to features?", "a": "STIX export excluded from current loop, light theme removed, snooze removed, Investigation Score removed\u2014documented non-goals. I prefer deleting misleading UI over maintaining half-honest paths."},
            {"q": "What is your testing philosophy?", "a": "Default SQLite pytest for speed; Postgres path before merging db/ changes. verify-local as merge gate. Playwright smoke optional. Tests assert behavior operators see\u2014job lock maps, EPSS skip, Sigma index read path."},
            {"q": "How do you design for self-hosters with no API keys?", "a": "Core CVE feed, RSS, and search work offline from public feeds. Empty states explain missing VT/GreyNoise keys without looking broken. Keys enhance; they do not gate login."},
            {"q": "Tell me about UX debt you paid down.", "a": "Forge honesty PRs: no fake 'ranked for your stack', real EmptyState on sparse ATT&amp;CK matrix, community-Sigma-first Detect. I treat analyst trust as a feature\u2014wrong detection is worse than no detection."},
            {"q": "How do you manage LLM cost risk?", "a": "Router failover, pacing headroom, empty-payload skip, ai_operations metering without storing prompts. LLM defaults off for detection context; deterministic Nuclei path default on."},
            {"q": "What would you do differently starting over?", "a": "I might stamp Postgres-only earlier\u2014but SQLite test fallback still saves CI minutes. I'd also centralize model catalog from day one; we recovered from stale OpenRouter IDs with SSOT in <code>model_catalog.py</code>."},
            {"q": "How do you onboard a new contributor quickly?", "a": "CLAUDE.md rulebook, HANDOVER newest-first, graphify/study-guide for architecture. Danger zones call out scheduler lock strings, migration forward-only, and request-path heavy work prohibition."},
            {"q": "Describe coordinating UI and backend changes.", "a": "ADR-002 scoring shipped API-first\u2014frontend displays <code>/risk</code> only. Drawer bundle reduced chatty fetches. I resist duplicating business logic in React; it always drifts."},
            {"q": "How do you handle security findings?", "a": "Fail closed in production: JWT required, admin key removed, SSRF blocks expanded, session revalidation. Security posture page gives analysts read-only transparency without duplicating admin corpus editing."},
            {"q": "What metric would you track if you had more time?", "a": "Time-to-triage for stack-matched KEV CVEs\u2014proxy via feed sort + OP accuracy feedback. Today we expose operational signals (backlog notifications, feed health) more than product analytics."},
            {"q": "Why dark terminal aesthetic?", "a": "Analysts live in terminals and SOC walls; light mode was noise. Tokens and Radix gave accessibility without Material blandness. Density-first\u2014no hero marketing columns."},
            {"q": "How do you decide when to add Procrastinate vs APScheduler?", "a": "Durable when failure is expensive and retry semantics matter\u2014stack backfill, LLM product extraction. Cron ingest stays APScheduler with locks\u2014simpler mental model for operators."},
